On Sat, 30 Sep 2000, Greggory S. LaBerge wrote:

> 
> To members of the list:
> 
> I have a n X n distance matrix from 37 human populations that summarises
> genetic allele frequency data. Zeros are on the diagonal and the matrix is
> square. I am trying to read this data into mclust and perform model based
> clustering analysis and compare to Ward's method and Average linkage methods
> of cluster analysis. 

mclust (like kmeans) works with an n x p matrix of n objects in p
dimensions, NOT an n x n distance matrix.

> I cannot get mclust to read this dataset. The error
> message is as follows:
> 
> Error in .Fortran: Cannot coerce mode list to integer: .Data = list(..

That sort of error usually means that you have a data frame when you think
you have a matrix.  However, here we can only guess at what arguments you
passed to mclust.

> I get this message when I try to execute the mclust command. I also get the
> message when trying to recreate the example of republican votes given in the
> help section of S-Plus under classification by mclust.

Works for me as written in that help section.  It is helpful when sending
problems like that to report *exactly* what you used.

> My system information:
> 
> Wintel PC 733 MHz
> 256MB RAM
> SPlus 2000 Professional Release 3

