You can't. You don't have any data to test distributional properties with,
as I said before.  Distances are not data.

> need to create an Splus dataset with my original raw data which is nxp,
> however due to the dataset complexity and my rather naive abilities with
> Splus it will take some time I am afraid.

You will, and the data will need to be continuous variates too.
 
> The example given in the help section was entered as it apprears. I still
> get the error. Is it possible that some defaults in my package may be
> causing this problem. I have also downloaded updated mclust algorithms from
> Fraley and Raftery but have not been able to use them due to errors.

It's highly unlikely, but it is quite possible that you have overridden a
system function.  Try masked() or conflicts() (after reading their help of
course).  Or try in a new working directory.

The thing to realize is that if you cut-and-paste an example and get an
error, it is very likely due to something you have done.  And if you want
to report an error, do give the exact input, the exact error message and
the result of traceback() at least.

