On Mon, 2 Oct 2000 aczarn at cs.uwa.edu.au wrote:

> 
> to anyone who can assist
> 
> i have just run the following anova analysis:
> 
> galgOA3<-aov(generationFirstAt1.0E.6~(crValueO*muValueO + 
> Error(seedPopulationF)), data = galgO)
> 
> i then proceeded to try and obtain adjusted means
> and means via the following commands
> 
> model.tables.aov(galgOA3,type="adj.means")
> 
> model.tables.aov(galgOA3,type="means")
> 
> in both instances though these commands have failed
> viz
> 
> model.tables.aov(galgOA3,type="adj.means")
> Problem in model.means.default(x, estimable.function..: model.means 
> is not implemented for class aov
> list
> 
> AND
> 
> model.tables.aov(galgOA3,type="means")
> Warning messages:
>   Model was refit to allow projection in: model.tables.aov(galgOA3, 
> type =
>         "means")
> Problem in [: No dim attribute for array subset: structure(.Data = 
> list(value = structure(.Data = c(
> 43.135105263158,        43.13....
> 
> can anyone suggest what may be going wrong ???

Yes. You should (almost) *never* call a method directly like this. The
function is model.tables, and a fit from an aov model with multiple strata
is of class "aovlist", not "aov".

Try

model.tables(galgOA3, type="means")

and look at the examples on the help page for model.tables.aov.

