Look at the S code. Mine says

        if((n.bad <- nrow(x) - sum(ok)) != 0)
                warning(paste(n.bad, "non-finite observations deleted"))

so any row with any NA, Inf or -Inf (or NaN) value in any x, y, or weights
is dropped (as the help page says).

> Is it affecting my output?
> If so, what do I do to correct the problem?

It's dropping rows with NAs, as it must. I don't believe that you
should have seen examples with NAs in and not seen this message.

Here's an example:

xx <- evap.x
xx[13, 3] <- NA
z1 <- stepwise(xx, evap.y)
Warning messages:
  1 non-finite observations deleted in: stepwise(xx, evap.y)

