Subject: Summary: netCDF data
Message-ID: <3.0.6.32.20001004122002.009dbad0@popserver.sfu.ca>

2 days ago I asked whether anyone had written S-plus functions to read
netCDF files. I have received several requests for a summary but no
positive response. 

Steve Wofsy pointed me to Noesys, a commercial product that can export
netCDF files as text files, but not as S-Plus files. 

There is an abundance of free software to  manipulate and visualize netCDF
files (see http://www.unidata.ucar.edu/packages/netcdf/software.html), most
of which run under UNIX, but few that export to any other file formats. 

MATLAB functions are available to read netCDF files into the MATLAB version
of a multidimensional 'array', and FERRET, a visualization tool developed
at the Pacific Marine Environmental Laboratory, will save subsets of data
as ASCII files. FERRET was written for UNIX, but a (pre-beta) PC version
that requires an X-windows emulator is also available, and seems to work
fine. As I only need to extract a limited amount of mostly 2-dimensional
data I opted for that route.

