An Splus/R library for the analysis of spatial point patterns
is now available at

        http://www.maths.uwa.edu.au/~adrian/spatstat.html

Its main functionality is to
     - display and manipulate two-dimensional point patterns 
     - estimate the summary functions F, G, K and J 
     - fit a point process model to a point pattern dataset 
        using maximum pseudolikelihood. 

A wide class of point process models is supported. They are described
in a syntax analogous to glm() and gam(). For example 

         mpl(data, ~ lo(x,y), Strauss(0.1), .....) 

will fit a point process model with a smooth spatial trend
and a Strauss-type pairwise interaction. 

