There were a few issues relating to the s-news mailing list that I wanted
to mention.

First, it appears I was a little incomplete about how to create an alias
for your subscribed address.  For those who may have missed the original
explanation, the reason for setting address aliases is that posting to the
s-news mailing list has been restricted to subscribers.  Setting an alias
is one way to add an extra address that is allowed to post also.  The
standard way of setting this is to send a message from the address that is
subscribed to mj2 at lists.biostat.wustl.edu that contains this in the body:

   alias MyNewAddress

Unfortunately some people's addresses may have changed so that they can
still receive mail at the old address, but mail always goes out from the
new one.  They way around this is to send this instead:

   default user MyOldAddress
   alias MyNewAddress

You'll need to accept any tokens that get sent to you.  Note that you can
put multiple "alias" commands in a single message - the "default user"
command will apply to all of them.  Also I've been adding some aliases for
some addresses as posts come in when I can figure out which subscribed
addresses they go with.  This is not something I anticipate that I'll
continue to do unless a user needs help.

A second issue is that the digest changed to being in MIME format since
this is now the internet standard.  A couple of users who have contacted
me have had trouble handling the MIME, so I've added an option to have a
plain text digest also.  You can change your digest setting by sending
this command:

   set s-news digest-plain MyAddress

The MIME digest will continue to be the default type of digest.

