> data which I need to reduce in size for some statistical routines I wish to
> run.  In order to keep the appropriate data, I need to use stratified
> sampling.  This will allow me to produce a sampled data frame which reflects
> roughly the same proportions of records having the same column values for
> those columns which need to be used in the stratification.
> 
> I have used the random sampling in S-PLUS before and it works fine.  But, I
> do not know of a stratified sampling routine available in S-PLUS.  Has
> anyone written one?  Is one available in an add-on library?  I know that SAS
> Enterprise Miner has a stratified sampling routine, so I figured that S-PLUS
> would have one as well.

Stratified sampling is just random sampling within strata. Exactly
how to do this depends on big the dataset is, how it is organized, how
the strata are defined, etc.  But at its simplest something like

unlist(lapply(split(1:nrow(df), df$strata), 
       function(x) sample(x, round(0.1*length(x)))

will give the indices of a 10% sample of a data frame df stratified
on a column `strata'.  If I've got this right it takes the row numbers,
splits them into strata, rnadom samples from each and makes the list back
into a vector.

