> SAS
> > Enterprise Miner has a stratified sampling routine, so I figured that
> S-PLUS
> > would have one as well.
> 
> Stratified sampling is just random sampling within strata. Exactly
> how to do this depends on big the dataset is, how it is organized, how
> the strata are defined, etc.  But at its simplest something like
> 
> unlist(lapply(split(1:nrow(df), df$strata), 
>        function(x) sample(x, round(0.1*length(x)))
> 
> will give the indices of a 10% sample of a data frame df stratified
> on a column `strata'.  If I've got this right it takes the row numbers,
> splits them into strata, rnadom samples from each and makes the list back
> into a vector.
