> Can you make sense of this?  Is there a correct version of dates( )?
> Will the next release make the correction?
> 
> > dates(c("03/24/00","01/01/00"),century=1901)
> [1] 03/24/2000 01/01/2000
> > dates(c("NA","01/01/00","03/24/00"),century=1901)
> [1] NA         NA         03/24/2000
> > dates(c("NA","03/24/00","01/01/00"),century=1901)
> [1] NA         NA         01/01/2000
> 
> This order dependence of the result doesn't look like a feature to me,
> and prepending with NA certainly should not make a difference.
> 
> Here's a slightly different example-- the placement of NA makes the
> difference:
> 
> > dates(c("NA","01/01/00","03/24/99"))
> [1] NA         NA         03/24/1999
> > dates(c("01/01/00","NA","03/24/99"))
> [1] 01/01/2000 NA         03/24/1999
> 
> To spice up the discussion, here's a related "Y2K" phenomenon:
> 
> > dates(c("NA","03/24/99","01/01/00"),century=1901)
> [1] NA         03/24/1999 NA 
> > dates(c("NA","03/24/99","01/01/99"),century=1901)
> Error in convert.dates: Missing value where logical needed: if(any(use))
>  yy[use] <- yy[use] + 100
