Steven Kaluzny of MathSoft sent me this message which has answered my
question (bottom) quite nicely. I re-post it with his permission. 

Ray Brownrigg also sent a message to the list which I reprint. It, too,
seems to answer my question.

Thanks to both!

(Steven Kaluzny's answer)

The tools required to build the world map database (or any other map
database) for use with library maps are not available under Windows/NT.

The map data does not go into an S-PLUS object so the data.dump() and
data.restore() functions can not be used for this data.  The library
uses a binary database that the functions know how to access.

I have built a Windows/NT version of the world map database (along with
versions for Unix). They are available via ftp:

        ftp://ftp.statsci.com/pub/support/maps

You will want the world.zip file there.

-Stephen Kaluzny
 MathSoft

