** From Nick Ellis ***
----------------------------------------------------------------
You can remove the inner loop with lapply or sapply. Your example
would look
like this:
> for(x in 1:(length(xy)-1)) {
>        temp[x,(x+1):length(xy)] <-
>                       sapply(
>                               xy[(x+1):length(xy)],
>                               function(w,z)
>                                       min(find.neighbor(z,quad.tree(w))[,3]),
>                               z = xy[[x]])
>               }

See below for an example.

(As I don't have the SpatialStats module, I constructed the example using
a
function that finds the nearest distance between two sets of points.)

> find.smallest.dist <- function(xy1, xy2)
{
        xy1 <- complex(real = xy1[[1]], imag = xy1[[2]])
        xy2 <- complex(real = xy2[[1]], imag = xy2[[2]])
        dis <- outer(xy1, xy2, function(x, y) abs(x - y))
        min(dis)
}
