Many thanks to all who responded.
In my original question (included below), I tried to ask how to get the
contrast matrix for interactions in a fully crossed anova. I think I was
a little unclear, but as a result, received lots of good information.

For contrasts of interactions I had tried ?contrasts(A*B)?. Bill Dunlop
and Bill Venables explained that to get interactions in this context I
needed ?interactions()?, so that statement should read ?contrasts(
interactions( A, B ) )?. Bill Venables explained that the meaning of ?*?
is context sensitive. Using ?:? did not help.

Brian Ripley and Bill Venables also intuited that I might want the
entire model matrix, in which case the appropriate command would be
?model.matrix(~ A * B)?

Thank you all very much,
Henry

