From: ripley at stats.ox.ac.uk (Prof Brian Ripley)
Date: Mon, 16 Oct 2000 13:35:25 +0100
Subject: Re: Covariance matrix
Message-ID: <200010161235.NAA29267@toucan.stats.ox.ac.uk>

> From: yye at safat.kisr.edu.kw
> Date: Mon, 16 Oct 2000 13:28:30 +0300
> 
> Dear S+ users,
> 
> Is there a simple way to get the variance-covariance matrix for the
> parameters with nls in S+?

The nls method for generic function vcov in library MASS. It's
not too hard:

> vcov.nls
function(object)
{
        sm <- summary(object)
        sm$cov.unscaled * sm$sigma^2
}

