On Mon, 23 Oct 2000, Meinhard Ploner wrote:

> Is there an easy way to perform a stepwise (forward or backward 
> selection) proportional hazard regression analysis, using the log-
> lik. or another measures? In SAS it's implemented, but I hate 
> exporting data... and I ' ll miss there some other features.

Use stepAIC in library MASS.  You can't use log-likelihoods with coxph (no
estimate of the hazard rate) but you can use partial log-likelihoods.
There's even a worked example in V&R.

